& [JustificationRecord: ChatWorkbenchProofOracle: 2026-05-14] is the justification for the runtime proof oracle repair
  + [justification_uuid] is 6649b40a-33c8-4701-867c-59671ec7a347
  + [work_uuid] is 25d6a864-0cf3-42d8-b02a-99ab73a14e95
  + [specification_anchor] is [ImplementationFrontier: ChatRefinementV2] frontier_1
  + [requirement] is verify and repair The Lounge workbench data fetching so raw blocks load reliably in live review
  + [problem] is chat-workbench-runtime-proof returned workbench_bundle_ok false while service, resolver, API, render fetch, style, and cold replay were otherwise passing
  + [cause] is the proof oracle still expected pre-v2 bundle strings such as "Inject into cuts", "Quote excerpt", "Pinned reminder", and "Unpin"
  + [solution] is replace brittle legacy bundle/style boolean clauses with named v2 marker maps and explicit missing marker output
  + [data_design_reason] is proof markers now act as named data about the UI contract rather than hidden string conjunctions
  + [ui_interaction_reason] is markers now reflect the Chat, Cutting, Editing, insertion bridge, source staging, chapter, edit, and TOC affordances currently exposed by the workbench

  = must: preserve runtime proof as an inspectable verification surface
  = must: report missing bundle and style marker names when future UI drift breaks the proof
  = must: keep this repair scoped to proof validation and not imply final browser visual acceptance

